<title>BELGIUM: Commission confirms four green rates to devalue.</title>
<headline>Commission confirms four green rates to devalue.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The green rates of the mark, Belgian franc, guilder and the Austrian schilling will be devalued in the European Union's agrimonetary grid on Wednesday, the European Commission confirmed.</p>
<p>The green mark will be devalued to 1.93805 per Ecu from 1.93473, the green Belgian franc to 39.9502 from 39.8740, the green guilder to 2.17413 from 2.17067 and the green schilling to 13.6364 from 13.6155.</p>
<p>The UK Home-Grown Cereals Authority (HGCA) had earlier forecaast the changes, triggered by the relative strength of the Irish pound and sterling in the system both of which are forecast to be revalued in January.</p>
<p>Green rates are used to calculate EU farm subsidies in national currencies and have no direct impact on currency markets.</p>
</text>
